  50: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  51:     """Extract and stack the contents between each row-aligned pair of 2x2 marker blocks.
  52: 
  53:     Input structure
  54:     - The grid contains noise plus one marker color whose components are all 2x2 blocks.
  55:     - The marker blocks occur as left/right pairs sharing the same two-row span.
  56: 
  57:     Rule
  58:     - For each paired marker span in top-to-bottom order, copy the rectangle strictly between the two marker blocks.
  59:     - Stack those copied rectangles vertically, discarding the markers and all cells outside the copied rectangles.
  60: 
  61:     Key insight
  62:     - The extraction markers are identifiable as the unique color made only of 2x2 components arranged in row-aligned pairs.
  63:     """
